            <fr:addr type="user">sss-0007</fr:addr>
            <fr:route>sss-0007.xml</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Closed Monoidal Structure">Closed Monoidal Structure</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <fr:p>A <fr:link href="sss-0006.xml" title="Monoidal Category" addr="sss-0006" type="local">monoidal category</fr:link> is <fr:em>left closed</fr:em> if for each <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Y \in  C]]></fr:tex>, the functor <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[- \otimes  Y : C \to  C]]></fr:tex> has a right adjoint <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[{Y} \multimap _L {-}  : C \to  C ]]></fr:tex> forming the left internal-hom out of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Y]]></fr:tex>.</fr:p>
            <fr:p>That is, for all <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[X,Y,Z]]></fr:tex>, there is a natural isomorphism <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[C[X \otimes  Y , Z] \cong  C[ X , [Y , Z]]]]></fr:tex></fr:p>
            <fr:p>There is an obvious right-handed variant <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[{Y} \multimap _R {-}]]></fr:tex> that is right adjoint to <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Y \otimes  -]]></fr:tex>. <fr:em>Note</fr:em>: this is likely better denoted with a flipped symbol, but I don't yet know if I can include it in Forester.</fr:p>
            <fr:p>If <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[C]]></fr:tex> is both right and left closed, the monoidal category is simply called <fr:em>closed</fr:em> (or perhaps <fr:em>biclosed</fr:em>).</fr:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
      </fr:mainmatter>
